From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: Intel XeSS stub libraries for games that ship them (Wine
 patch 0950)

EA Sports College Football 27 ships Intel's XeSS libraries (libxess.dll,
libxess_fg.dll, libxell.dll) and imports them statically: the PE loader
requires them to exist.  On the PS5's AMD GPU the game's own copies
initialise against no Intel driver and crash or return values the game
takes for valid.  Disabling them (=d) doesn't work because the loader
won't start the program without them (STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND, c0000135).

Wine patch 0950 adds stub builtins that export every public XeSS SDK
function but return XESS_RESULT_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_DEVICE (-1) from any
call that creates a context or initialises.  The game sees "no XeSS
hardware" and falls back to its other upscaler (FSR, native).  The title
overrides libxess, libxess_fg, libxell to builtin (=b) so Wine's copies
replace the game's.
